module

-- **OPEN.** Compiles, and contains a `sorry` that is **yours to discharge, in
-- this file**. Nothing will fill it in. A signature install leaves it alone.
--
-- **Non-vacuity** — that a well-formed model exists at all.
--
-- Easy to overlook and fatal to omit. Soundness says the assumptions of a
-- checked proof hold in *no* well-formed model. If `model_wf` were satisfied by
-- nothing, that would be true of every proof, and the whole development would
-- prove nothing while appearing to prove everything.
--
-- Could arrive proven: it asks for one model, and the obvious one — every
-- symbol mapped to the default value of its type — is generated. In Logos the
-- corresponding file constructs exactly that.
--
-- What this obligation cost Logos, and what shape the work takes, is in the
-- Logos experience report:
--   @EUDAIMONIA@/blob/main/docs/logos-experience-report.md
-- `SmtModel` directly rather than `ModelWf`: this statement does not need the
-- projections, and `ModelWf.lean` is one of the files `--theorems` can leave
-- out. A front-end theorem must not depend on another being generated.
public import @CALCULUS@.SmtModel
import all @CALCULUS@.SmtModel
public import @CALCULUS@.Proofs.TypeDefaults
import all @CALCULUS@.Proofs.TypeDefaults

@[expose] public section

namespace Smtm

/-!
The obligation is narrower than it looks, because `Proofs/TypeDefaults.lean`
already carries the hard half — and carries it *proven*.

`type_default_typed_of_inhabited` and `type_default_canonical_of_inhabited_wf_rec`
say that an **inhabited**, recursively well-formed type has a default value that
is both correctly typed and canonical. Those transfer unchanged from Logos.

What does not transfer is the step from "well formed" to "inhabited". That is a
fact about *your* types, so it is the sorry below. Logos proves it in
`Cpc/Proofs/TypePreservation/Support.lean`, which is 957 lines and genuinely
calculus-specific.
-/

/--
Every well-formed type is inhabited by a canonical value of that type.

**This is the real obligation.** With it, a model follows: map every symbol to
the default value of its type and the three conjuncts of `model_wf` are the two
proven theorems in `Proofs/TypeDefaults.lean` plus bookkeeping.
-/
theorem canonical_type_inhabited_of_type_wf (T : SmtType) :
    __smtx_type_wf T = true ->
    ∃ v : SmtValue, __smtx_typeof_value v = T ∧ __smtx_value_canonical v = true := by
  sorry

/--
Well-formed models exist.

Follows from the lemma above by constructing the model that maps each symbol to
a witness of its type. Logos builds it in
`Cpc/Proofs/TypePreservation/Nonvacuity.lean` -- 104 lines, and one of the six
files measured to be identical across its two packages, so this derivation is
not calculus-specific either and should eventually arrive proven.
-/
theorem model_wf_nonvacuous : ∃ M : SmtModel, model_wf M := by
  sorry

end Smtm
